    "6:00 am in inn: Rita spends the period at the inn. Phil says: Copy that, Rita. I'll have the temps and the groundhog quip lined up by 6:45. Don't worry about the evening—I've got that one o'clock coach ticket to burn and a couch to haul Wednesday, so I'll leave the seven to you and the town band. Six-fifty-five, phone return, two minutes, done. See you at the lobby. Phil spends the period at the inn. Rita invites Phil on the crew radio to contribute to the evening slot.",
    "9:30 am in inn: Rita spends the period at the inn. Phil says: Rita, I'm locked in—phone return at six-fifty, two minutes, no couch talk. I'll be on the line from the coach or the Pittsburgh side, just give me a ring. Thanks for the invite. Phil spends the period at the inn. Phil radios Rita and accepted the evening assignment."
   ]
